#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cold-videos: send finished camera videos older than a few days to off-site storage (decision A1, as the
owner changed it on Oct 30, 2026, when the cold drive failed).

  cold-videos [--keep-days N] [--wait MIN] [--max-mb-s MB] [--limit N] [--dry-run] [--archive DIR]
  cold-videos --bring-back REL [REL ...] [--archive DIR]

Each finished camera day older than --keep-days (cameras/video/<id>/<year>/<id>-<day>.mp4 and the .csv beside
it, plugins/cameras/ingest/camera_video.py's layout) is sent to off-site storage (Backblaze B2, encrypted) and
read back from there. Only when the sha256 of what came back is the original's is the original replaced, in one
rename, by an off-site link: a symlink whose target, offsite:<bytes>:<sha256>, leads nowhere and records what was
sent. No second local copy is kept. Readers keep the same path: the roll-up counts a linked day as done, and the
library's index marks it "offsite", which the library shows as kept off-site.

Off-site storage is reached through one command, OFFSITE_SSH in heavy.conf (on the VM, an ssh to one locked-down
command outside the VM, which holds the storage's keys: the VM holds none), with a verb after it:
  ping                          "ok" once the storage answers
  list                          "<bytes>\t<rel>" for each camera file it holds
  put <rel> <bytes> <mtime_ns>  the file on stdin; answers "ok <sha256 of what arrived>". A file already there
                                with other bytes is refused, not replaced
  verify                        <rel> lines on stdin; answers "<sha256>  <rel>" for each one read back in full
                                from the storage (one it doesn't hold, or couldn't read, is left out)
  get <rel>                     the file's bytes on stdout
<rel> is relative to the camera archive: video/<id>/<year>/<name>, the layout the cold drive had.

Each run then lists what the storage holds and checks every off-site link against it (the file there, with the
bytes in the link), so a copy that goes missing later shows in status. It also checks the links the cold drive
left (days moved there before Oct 30, which lead nowhere now): when the storage holds a file with the size this
tool logged when it moved it to the drive, the file is read back, and if its sha256 is the logged one, its link
becomes an off-site link. One that doesn't match, or that the storage doesn't hold yet, keeps its old link and is
counted; one that didn't match is read back again only once its size there changes, or a week later.

  --keep-days N   finished days kept on the VM's disk (default 7, or COLD_VIDEO_KEEP_DAYS): a day goes once it's
                  more than N days old. At least 2, so today's and yesterday's files are never touched.
  --wait MIN      wait at most MIN minutes for the roll-up to finish (default 0: refuse at once)
  --max-mb-s MB   read the VM's disk at most this fast (default 50)
  --limit N       send at most N files and leave the old links alone (a careful first run)
  --dry-run       say what would be sent and what stays; change nothing
  --archive DIR   the camera archive (default /srv/tvt/archive/cameras)
  --bring-back REL ...
                  fetch these off-site files back onto the VM's disk (REL as above, or a path in the archive),
                  with the other file of each camera-day, each checked against the bytes and sha256 in its link
                  before it replaces the link. A day older than --keep-days goes off-site again on the next run.

When it sends:
- once tonight's camera roll-up has finished: at night both capture status files say rolling_up false after
  00:05, in the day neither says it's rolling up. It holds the roll-up's own lock (cameras/rollup.lock) while it
  works, so no roll-up starts meanwhile;
- not from 23:55 until tonight's roll-up has finished, nor within 15 minutes of a planned VM restart
  (MAINTENANCE): a run under way stops between files, and no step it starts may run past the next 23:55;
- never a day whose JPEGs are still in the buffer (cameras/jpeg/<id>/<day>), whose encode is going (a .part
  beside it), a file written in the last 10 minutes, or a CSV without its video.

A day's video goes before its CSV, so a day half sent shows as off-site. Idempotent and resumable: a sent file is
a link, and is skipped. One sent but not yet read back and linked when a run stopped is sent again by the next
(the storage keeps the copy it has when the bytes are the same).

Settings, in /srv/tvt/work/heavy.conf (KEY=value; the VM's own, kept out of the repo): OFFSITE_SSH, the command
(split as a shell would), and optionally COLD_VIDEO_KEEP_DAYS.

Log: each file sent or relinked (path, bytes, sha256) and each run's start and end, on stdout (the journal, under
systemd) and appended to cameras/cold-videos.log; the last run's outcome in cameras/cold-videos.json, which
bin/status reads. The log is also where the old links' sha256s are read from: keep it.

Exit: 0 done (or nothing to send); 1 a file failed its check (its original is kept), or the storage's list
failed; 2 usage or settings; 69 the off-site storage can't be reached; 75 not now (the roll-up is going or hasn't
finished, a restart is planned, another run is going, or 23:55 came); 130 interrupted.

Runs daily from deploy/systemd/tvt-cold-videos.timer, as the archive's owner. Source: deploy/bin/cold-videos in
the repo; installed in /srv/tvt/work/bin beside heavy, whose rules and settings it reads, so the two always agree.
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import fcntl
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import signal
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
from collections import Counter

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))


def load_heavy(path=None):
    """heavy, from beside this file (or path), as a module: its rules, paths and settings."""
    path = path or os.path.join(HERE, "heavy")
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("heavy_for_cold_videos", path)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


heavy = load_heavy()

KEEP_DAYS = 7                   # finished days kept on the VM's disk (decision A1: "older than about 7 days")
MIN_KEEP_DAYS = 2               # so today's and yesterday's files are never touched
MAX_MB_S = 50.0                 # the VM's disk is capped at 120 MB/s, shared with the capture and the database
CHUNK = 4 * 2**20
STOP_AT = dt.time(23, 55)       # tonight's roll-up starts at 00:05
RESTART_MARGIN = dt.timedelta(minutes=15)
RECENT_S = 600                  # a file written this recently is left alone
WAIT_POLL_S = 60
ANSWER_S = 120                  # how long the storage gets to answer, besides moving the bytes
MIN_RATE = 0.5e6                # bytes a second below which a transfer counts as stalled
OLD_BATCH = 500                 # old cold-drive links read back together, at most,
OLD_BATCH_BYTES = 2**30         # and at most this many bytes
RECHECK = dt.timedelta(days=7)  # an old link whose copy didn't match is read back again after this
SHOW = 20                       # problems of one kind logged one by one, at most
BACK_SPARE_GB = 1               # left free on the VM's disk above heavy's floor when a file comes back
NAME = re.compile(r"^(?P<cam>.+)-(?P<day>\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d)\.(?P<ext>mp4|csv)$")
REL = re.compile(r"video/(?P<cam>[^/]+)/(?P<year>\d{4})/(?P=cam)-(?P=year)-\d\d-\d\d\.(?:mp4|csv)")
MOVED = re.compile(r" moved (?P<rel>video/\S+) \((?P<bytes>\d+) bytes, sha256 (?P<sha>[0-9a-f]{64})\)")
OFFSITE = "offsite:"            # an off-site link's target: offsite:<bytes>:<sha256> (camera_video.OFFSITE_LINK)
OFFSITE_TARGET = re.compile(r"offsite:(?P<bytes>\d+):(?P<sha>[0-9a-f]{64})")
ROLLUP_LOCK = "rollup.lock"     # camera_video.LOCK: held by a roll-up while it runs
LOCK = "cold-videos.lock"
LOG = "cold-videos.log"
STATE = "cold-videos.json"
LINK = ".cold-link"             # a symlink about to replace an original (hidden, beside it)
BACK = ".cold-back"             # a file coming back from off-site storage (hidden, beside its link)

EX_FAILED, EX_USAGE, EX_UNREACHABLE, EX_LATER, EX_INT = 1, 2, 69, 75, 130
RESULTS = {0: "done", EX_FAILED: "failed", EX_USAGE: "settings", EX_UNREACHABLE: "off-site storage unreachable",
           EX_LATER: "not now", EX_INT: "interrupted"}


class Stop(Exception):
    """The run can't start, or can't go on: why, and the exit code. record: whether the state
    file takes it (not when another run is going: that run records its own)."""

    def __init__(self, message, code, record=True):
        super().__init__(message)
        self.code = code
        self.record = record


class Terminated(Exception):
    """SIGTERM (systemd stopping the run): stop between reads, leaving the original in place."""


class CheckFailed(Exception):
    """One file couldn't be sent safely; its original is kept."""


class OffsiteError(CheckFailed):
    """The off-site storage didn't do what it was asked, or didn't answer."""


def stamp(t=None):
    return (t or dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)).astimezone(dt.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def gb(n):
    return n / heavy.GB


def last_line(data):
    text = data.decode(errors="replace") if isinstance(data, bytes) else (data or "")
    lines = [line.strip() for line in text.splitlines() if line.strip()]
    return lines[-1][:300] if lines else "no message"


def moving(nbytes, transfers=1):
    """Seconds a step that moves nbytes (transfers times over) may take before it counts as stalled."""
    return ANSWER_S + transfers * nbytes / MIN_RATE


# --- off-site storage -------------------------------------------------------------

class Watchdog:
    """Kills proc once timeout seconds have passed (a stalled transfer), and says so."""

    def __init__(self, proc, timeout):
        self.fired = threading.Event()

        def kill():
            self.fired.set()
            proc.kill()

        self.timer = threading.Timer(timeout, kill)
        self.timer.daemon = True
        self.timer.start()

    def cancel(self):
        self.timer.cancel()


class Offsite:
    """Off-site storage: the command in OFFSITE_SSH, with a verb after it (see the top)."""

    def __init__(self, command):
        self.command = list(command)

    def call(self, verb, *args, data=None, timeout=ANSWER_S):
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(self.command + [verb, *args], input=data, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                               stderr=subprocess.PIPE, timeout=timeout)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            raise OffsiteError(f"{verb}: no answer in {timeout:.0f} s")
        except OSError as err:
            raise OffsiteError(f"{verb}: {err}")
        if r.returncode:
            raise OffsiteError(f"{verb}: exit {r.returncode}: {last_line(r.stderr)}")
        return r.stdout.decode(errors="replace")

    def ping(self):
        self.call("ping")

    def listing(self, timeout):
        """{rel: bytes} for each camera file the storage holds."""
        held = {}
        for line in self.call("list", timeout=timeout).splitlines():
            size, _, rel = line.partition("\t")
            if size.isdigit() and REL.fullmatch(rel):
                held[rel] = int(size)
        return held

    def verify(self, rels, timeout):
        """{rel: sha256 of its copy, read back in full from the storage} for those of rels it could
        read back. One left out is not proven."""
        want = set(rels)
        out = self.call("verify", data="".join(rel + "\n" for rel in rels).encode(), timeout=timeout)
        back = {}
        for line in out.splitlines():
            digest, _, rel = line.partition("  ")
            if rel in want and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}", digest):
                back[rel] = digest
        return back

    def put(self, path, rel, st, pace, timeout):
        """Sends the file at path as rel. Returns its sha256, computed as it was read. Raises
        CheckFailed when what arrived isn't what was sent, OffsiteError when it wasn't taken."""
        h = hashlib.sha256()
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen(self.command + ["put", rel, str(st.st_size), str(st.st_mtime_ns)],
                                    stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
        except OSError as err:
            raise OffsiteError(f"put: {err}")
        dog = Watchdog(proc, timeout)
        try:
            try:
                with open(path, "rb", buffering=0) as f:
                    while chunk := f.read(CHUNK):
                        h.update(chunk)
                        proc.stdin.write(chunk)
                        pace(len(chunk))
            except BrokenPipeError:
                pass                                     # it stopped reading: its answer says why
            out, err = proc.communicate()
        except BaseException:
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            raise
        finally:
            dog.cancel()
        if dog.fired.is_set():
            raise OffsiteError(f"put: given up after {timeout:.0f} s")
        if proc.returncode:
            raise OffsiteError(f"put: exit {proc.returncode}: {last_line(err)}")
        words = out.decode(errors="replace").split()
        if len(words) != 2 or words[0] != "ok":
            raise OffsiteError(f"put: an answer it doesn't understand: {out[:200]!r}")
        if words[1] != h.hexdigest():
            raise CheckFailed("what arrived off-site isn't what was sent (its sha256 differs)")
        return h.hexdigest()

    def get(self, rel, f, pace, timeout):
        """Writes rel's bytes from the storage to f. Returns (bytes, sha256)."""
        h, n = hashlib.sha256(), 0
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen(self.command + ["get", rel], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
        except OSError as err:
            raise OffsiteError(f"get: {err}")
        dog = Watchdog(proc, timeout)
        try:
            while chunk := proc.stdout.read(CHUNK):
                h.update(chunk)
                f.write(chunk)
                n += len(chunk)
                pace(len(chunk))
            err = proc.stderr.read()
            proc.wait()
        except BaseException:
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            raise
        finally:
            dog.cancel()
            proc.stdout.close()
            proc.stderr.close()
        if dog.fired.is_set():
            raise OffsiteError(f"get: given up after {timeout:.0f} s")
        if proc.returncode:
            raise OffsiteError(f"get: exit {proc.returncode}: {last_line(err)}")
        return n, h.hexdigest()


def offsite_settings():
    """The off-site storage, from heavy.conf. Raises Stop when it isn't set up."""
    text = heavy.settings().get("OFFSITE_SSH", "")
    if not text:
        raise Stop(f"{heavy.path('heavy.conf')} names no way to off-site storage (OFFSITE_SSH)", EX_USAGE)
    try:
        command = shlex.split(text)
    except ValueError as err:
        raise Stop(f"OFFSITE_SSH in heavy.conf can't be read: {err}", EX_USAGE)
    return Offsite(command)


def reachable(offsite):
    """Raises Stop when the off-site storage doesn't answer."""
    try:
        offsite.ping()
    except OffsiteError as err:
        raise Stop(f"the off-site storage can't be reached ({err})", EX_UNREACHABLE)


def keep_days_setting(given):
    if given is not None:
        return given
    try:
        return int(heavy.settings().get("COLD_VIDEO_KEEP_DAYS") or KEEP_DAYS)
    except ValueError:
        raise Stop("COLD_VIDEO_KEEP_DAYS in heavy.conf must be a whole number of days", EX_USAGE)


# --- when it may send -----------------------------------------------------------

def restart_problem(t):
    """Why a planned VM restart holds sends back, or None."""
    m = heavy.maintenance(t)
    if m is None:
        return None
    text, restart = m
    if restart is None:
        return f"MAINTENANCE gives no one restart time heavy can read ({text!r}), so nothing starts"
    if restart - t <= RESTART_MARGIN:
        return f"a VM restart is planned at {restart:%H:%M} Boise"
    return None


def gate(t, statuses):
    """None when sending may start at t (Boise), else why not. The roll-up rule is heavy's: at
    night, once both capture services report tonight's roll-up finished; in the day, while
    neither says it's rolling up."""
    clock = t.time()
    if clock >= STOP_AT or clock < heavy.NIGHT[0]:
        return (f"it's {heavy.hm(t)} in Boise: from {STOP_AT:%H:%M}, sends wait for tonight's camera "
                f"roll-up (from 00:05) to finish")
    going = heavy.rolling_now(t, statuses)
    if going:
        return f"the camera roll-up is still going ({', '.join(going)})"
    if clock < heavy.DAY[0]:
        done, why = heavy.rollup_finished(t, statuses)
        if not done:
            return why
    return restart_problem(t)


def deadline_after(t):
    """The next 23:55 (Boise) after t: no step of a run that started at t may go past it."""
    stop = dt.datetime.combine(t.date(), STOP_AT, t.tzinfo)
    return stop if t < stop else stop + dt.timedelta(days=1)


def stop_between_files(deadline):
    """Raises Stop once the run's 23:55 has come or a planned restart is near."""
    t = heavy.now()
    if t >= deadline:
        raise Stop(f"stopped at {heavy.hm(t)} Boise: tonight's roll-up comes next", EX_LATER)
    why = restart_problem(t)
    if why:
        raise Stop(f"stopped: {why}", EX_LATER)


def within(deadline, seconds):
    """seconds, cut to what's left before the run's 23:55. Raises Stop when nothing is left."""
    if deadline is None:
        return seconds
    left = (deadline - heavy.now()).total_seconds()
    if left <= 0:
        raise Stop(f"stopped at {heavy.hm(heavy.now())} Boise: tonight's roll-up comes next", EX_LATER)
    return min(seconds, left)


def take_lock(path):
    """An fd holding path's exclusive flock, or None when someone else holds it."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        os.close(fd)
        return None
    return fd


def wait_to_start(cameras, wait_min, say):
    """Waits (at most wait_min minutes) until sending may start, and returns an fd holding the
    roll-up's lock. Raises Stop when the wait runs out."""
    give_up = time.monotonic() + wait_min * 60
    said = None
    while True:
        why = gate(heavy.now(), heavy.read_statuses(os.path.join(cameras, "status")))
        if why is None:
            fd = take_lock(os.path.join(cameras, ROLLUP_LOCK))
            if fd is not None:
                return fd
            why = f"a camera roll-up holds {ROLLUP_LOCK}"
        left = give_up - time.monotonic()
        if left <= 0:
            raise Stop(why, EX_LATER)
        if why != said:
            say(f"waiting (at most {left / 60:.0f} min more): {why}")
            said = why
        time.sleep(min(WAIT_POLL_S, max(1.0, left)))


# --- what goes ------------------------------------------------------------------

def plan(cameras, cutoff, now_s=None):
    """(files to send, Counter of reasons files stay). Files are (path relative to the archive,
    bytes): video/<id>/<year>/<id>-<day>.ext, each camera-day's video before its CSV, oldest day
    first. Only regular files: a sent one is a symlink."""
    now_s = heavy.now().timestamp() if now_s is None else now_s
    base = os.path.join(cameras, "video")
    todo, kept = [], Counter()
    try:
        with os.scandir(base) as it:
            cams = sorted(e.name for e in it if e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return [], kept
    for cam in cams:
        with os.scandir(os.path.join(base, cam)) as it:
            years = sorted(e.name for e in it if e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False) and e.name.isdigit())
        for year in years:
            if int(year) > cutoff.year:
                continue
            with os.scandir(os.path.join(base, cam, year)) as it:
                entries = {e.name: e for e in it}
            for name, entry in entries.items():
                m = NAME.match(name)
                if not m or m["cam"] != cam:
                    continue
                try:
                    day = dt.date.fromisoformat(m["day"])
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if day > cutoff or entry.is_symlink():
                    continue
                try:
                    st = entry.stat(follow_symlinks=False)
                except OSError:
                    continue
                if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                    continue
                video = f"{cam}-{day.isoformat()}.mp4"
                if video + ".part" in entries:
                    kept["its encode is going"] += 1
                elif m["ext"] == "csv" and video not in entries:
                    kept["a CSV without its video"] += 1
                elif os.path.lexists(os.path.join(cameras, "jpeg", cam, day.isoformat())):
                    kept["its JPEGs are still in the buffer"] += 1
                elif now_s - st.st_mtime < RECENT_S:
                    kept["written in the last 10 minutes"] += 1
                else:
                    todo.append((day, cam, m["ext"] == "csv", f"video/{cam}/{year}/{name}", st.st_size))
    todo.sort()
    return [(rel, size) for _, _, _, rel, size in todo], kept


def links(cameras):
    """{rel: target} for each camera file in the archive that's a symlink."""
    out = {}
    for folder, dirs, names in os.walk(os.path.join(cameras, "video")):
        dirs.sort()
        for name in names:
            path = os.path.join(folder, name)
            rel = os.path.relpath(path, cameras)
            if REL.fullmatch(rel) and os.path.islink(path):
                out[rel] = os.readlink(path)
    return out


def logged(cameras):
    """{rel: (bytes, sha256)} as this tool last moved each file to the cold drive, from its log."""
    out = {}
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(cameras, LOG), errors="replace") as f:
            for line in f:
                m = MOVED.search(line)
                if m:
                    out[m["rel"]] = (int(m["bytes"]), m["sha"])
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    return out


def sibling(rel):
    """The other file of rel's camera-day: its CSV for a video, its video for a CSV."""
    return rel[:-4] + (".csv" if rel.endswith(".mp4") else ".mp4")


# --- sending one file -------------------------------------------------------------

class Pace:
    """Keeps reads under a rate (bytes a second), counted over the whole run."""

    def __init__(self, mb_s):
        self.rate = mb_s * 1e6
        self.start = time.monotonic()
        self.done = 0

    def __call__(self, n):
        if self.rate <= 0:
            return
        self.done += n
        ahead = self.done / self.rate - (time.monotonic() - self.start)
        if ahead > 0:
            time.sleep(ahead)


def fsync_dir(path):
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_DIRECTORY", 0))
    except OSError:
        return
    try:
        os.fsync(fd)
    except OSError:
        pass
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def hidden(path, suffix):
    folder, name = os.path.split(path)
    return os.path.join(folder, "." + name + suffix)


def offsite_target(size, sha):
    return f"{OFFSITE}{size}:{sha}"


def put_link(path, target):
    """Puts a symlink to target where path is, in one rename: readers see the file (or the old
    link) or the new link, never neither."""
    link = hidden(path, LINK)
    if os.path.lexists(link):
        os.remove(link)
    os.symlink(target, link)
    os.replace(link, path)
    fsync_dir(os.path.dirname(path))


def send(rel, cameras, offsite, pace, deadline):
    """Sends one file, reads it back, and once its copy off-site is the original, replaces it with
    its off-site link. Returns (lstat, sha256), or None when it's no longer a regular file."""
    src = os.path.join(cameras, rel)
    st = os.lstat(src)
    if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
        return None
    sha = offsite.put(src, rel, st, pace, within(deadline, moving(st.st_size, 2)))
    back = offsite.verify([rel], within(deadline, moving(st.st_size))).get(rel)
    if back is None:
        raise CheckFailed("it couldn't be read back from the off-site storage after it was sent")
    if back != sha:
        raise CheckFailed("the copy read back from the off-site storage doesn't match the original's sha256")
    now = os.lstat(src)
    if (now.st_ino, now.st_size, now.st_mtime_ns) != (st.st_ino, st.st_size, st.st_mtime_ns):
        raise CheckFailed("the original changed while it was sent; it stays, and the next run sends it again")
    put_link(src, offsite_target(st.st_size, sha))
    return st, sha


# --- a run --------------------------------------------------------------------

class Run:
    def __init__(self, cameras, dry_run):
        self.cameras = cameras
        self.dry_run = dry_run
        self.started = dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)
        self.moved = self.bytes = self.failed = self.left = 0
        self.relinked = self.old_left = self.old_bad = self.old_unknown = 0
        self.offsite_links = self.offsite_missing = None
        self.kept = Counter()
        self.cutoff = self.deadline = None
        self.bad_seen = {}                       # old links whose copy didn't match: {rel: [bytes, day checked]}

    def say(self, message):
        line = f"{stamp()} {message}"
        print(line, flush=True)
        if not self.dry_run:
            try:
                with open(os.path.join(self.cameras, LOG), "a") as f:
                    f.write(line + "\n")
            except OSError as err:
                print(f"{stamp()} (the log can't be written: {err})", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)

    def previous(self):
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(self.cameras, STATE)) as f:
                return json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return {}

    def finish(self, code, why="", record=True):
        """Logs the end and records it in the state file (unless record is false). Returns code."""
        result = RESULTS.get(code, "failed")
        moved = f"sent {self.moved} files ({gb(self.bytes):.2f} GB) off-site"
        tail = (f"; {self.left} still to send" if self.left else "") + \
               (f"; {self.failed} failed their check" if self.failed else "") + \
               (f"; {self.offsite_missing} off-site links whose copy isn't there" if self.offsite_missing else "") + \
               (f"; {self.relinked} old cold-drive links now off-site links" if self.relinked else "") + \
               (f"; {self.old_left} files still link to the cold drive" if self.old_left else "") + \
               (f" ({self.old_bad} don't match off-site, {self.old_unknown} with no logged sha256)"
                if self.old_bad or self.old_unknown else "")
        self.say(f"{'dry run ' if self.dry_run else ''}{result}: {why + '; ' if why else ''}{moved}{tail}")
        if self.dry_run or not record:
            return code
        previous = self.previous()
        finished = stamp()
        state = {
            "version": 2, "started": stamp(self.started), "finished": finished, "code": code,
            "result": result, "why": why, "moved": self.moved, "bytes": self.bytes, "failed": self.failed,
            "left": self.left, "kept": dict(self.kept),
            "cutoff": self.cutoff.isoformat() if self.cutoff else None,
            "offsite_links": self.offsite_links, "offsite_missing": self.offsite_missing,
            "relinked": self.relinked, "old_left": self.old_left, "old_bad": self.old_bad,
            "old_unknown": self.old_unknown, "bad_seen": self.bad_seen or previous.get("bad_seen", {}),
            "last_done": finished if code == 0 else previous.get("last_done"),
        }
        path = os.path.join(self.cameras, STATE)
        try:
            with open(path + ".part", "w") as f:
                json.dump(state, f, indent=1)
            os.replace(path + ".part", path)
        except OSError as err:
            self.say(f"(the state file can't be written: {err})")
        return code


def parse(argv):
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="cold-videos", description="Send finished camera videos older than a few "
                                "days to off-site storage, leaving links (deploy/README.md).")
    p.add_argument("--keep-days", type=int, help=f"finished days kept on the VM's disk (default {KEEP_DAYS})")
    p.add_argument("--wait", type=float, default=0, metavar="MIN", help="wait at most MIN minutes for the roll-up")
    p.add_argument("--max-mb-s", type=float, default=MAX_MB_S, metavar="MB", help="read at most this fast")
    p.add_argument("--limit", type=int, metavar="N", help="send at most N files and leave the old links alone")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="say what would be sent; change nothing")
    p.add_argument("--archive", help="the camera archive (default: beside heavy's status files)")
    p.add_argument("--bring-back", nargs="+", metavar="REL", help="fetch these off-site files back")
    return p.parse_args(argv)


def send_new(files, cameras, offsite, pace, run_):
    """Sends files one at a time, each read back before it becomes a link."""
    gone = 0                                     # files no longer regular files when their turn came
    for rel, _ in files:
        run_.left = len(files) - run_.moved - gone       # if it stops here
        stop_between_files(run_.deadline)
        try:
            done = send(rel, cameras, offsite, pace, run_.deadline)
        except OffsiteError as err:
            run_.failed += 1
            run_.say(f"FAILED {rel}: {err} (the original stays)")
            reachable(offsite)                   # gone away: stop rather than fail every file
            continue
        except (CheckFailed, OSError) as err:
            run_.failed += 1
            run_.say(f"FAILED {rel}: {err} (the original stays)")
            continue
        if done is None:
            gone += 1
            continue
        st, sha = done
        run_.moved += 1
        run_.bytes += st.st_size
        run_.say(f"sent {rel} ({st.st_size} bytes, sha256 {sha})")
    run_.left = len(files) - run_.moved - gone


def audit(offsite_links, held, run_):
    """Counts the off-site links whose copy the storage doesn't hold with the bytes in the link."""
    missing = []
    for rel, target in sorted(offsite_links.items()):
        m = OFFSITE_TARGET.fullmatch(target)
        if not m or held.get(rel) != int(m["bytes"]):
            missing.append(rel)
    run_.offsite_links, run_.offsite_missing = len(offsite_links), len(missing)
    for rel in missing[:SHOW]:
        run_.say(f"MISSING off-site: {rel}: its link says {offsite_links[rel]}, the storage holds "
                 + (f"{held[rel]} bytes" if rel in held else "nothing"))
    if len(missing) > SHOW:
        run_.say(f"MISSING off-site: {len(missing) - SHOW} more")


def relink_old(olds, held, offsite, run_, bad_before):
    """Turns the cold drive's old links into off-site links, each once its copy read back from the
    storage has the sha256 this tool logged when it moved the file to the drive."""
    run_.old_left = len(olds)
    if not olds:
        return
    record = logged(run_.cameras)
    today = heavy.now().date()
    ready, waiting = [], 0
    for rel in sorted(olds):
        if rel not in record:
            run_.old_unknown += 1
        elif held.get(rel) != record[rel][0]:
            waiting += 1
        elif rel in bad_before and bad_before[rel][0] == held[rel] and \
                today - dt.date.fromisoformat(bad_before[rel][1]) < RECHECK:
            run_.old_bad += 1                    # didn't match lately, and nothing there changed
            run_.bad_seen[rel] = bad_before[rel]
        else:
            ready.append(rel)
    run_.say(f"{len(olds)} files still link to the cold drive: {len(ready)} held off-site, to read back now; "
             f"{waiting} not off-site yet" + (f"; {run_.old_bad} that didn't match lately" if run_.old_bad else "")
             + (f"; {run_.old_unknown} with no sha256 in {LOG}" if run_.old_unknown else ""))
    if run_.dry_run:
        return
    batches, batch, size = [], [], 0
    for rel in ready:
        if batch and (len(batch) >= OLD_BATCH or size + held[rel] > OLD_BATCH_BYTES):
            batches.append((batch, size))
            batch, size = [], 0
        batch.append(rel)
        size += held[rel]
    if batch:
        batches.append((batch, size))
    unread = 0
    for rels, size in batches:
        stop_between_files(run_.deadline)
        try:
            back = offsite.verify(rels, within(run_.deadline, moving(size)))
        except OffsiteError as err:
            run_.say(f"old links: {len(rels)} couldn't be read back ({err}); they keep their old links")
            reachable(offsite)
            continue
        for rel in rels:
            size_, sha = record[rel]
            got = back.get(rel)
            if got is None:
                unread += 1                      # not read back this time: tried again next run
                continue
            if got != sha:
                run_.old_bad += 1
                run_.bad_seen[rel] = [held[rel], today.isoformat()]
                if run_.old_bad <= SHOW:
                    run_.say(f"old link {rel}: its copy off-site doesn't match the sha256 logged when it moved to "
                             f"the cold drive ({sha}); it keeps its old link")
                continue
            path = os.path.join(run_.cameras, rel)
            if not os.path.islink(path) or os.readlink(path) != olds[rel]:
                continue                         # changed meanwhile (a day encoded again)
            put_link(path, offsite_target(size_, sha))
            run_.relinked += 1
            run_.old_left -= 1
            run_.say(f"relinked {rel} ({size_} bytes, sha256 {sha}): its copy off-site, read back")
    if unread:
        run_.say(f"old links: {unread} couldn't be read back this time; the next run tries them again")


def run(args, run_):
    cameras = run_.cameras
    offsite = offsite_settings()
    keep = keep_days_setting(args.keep_days)
    if keep < MIN_KEEP_DAYS:
        raise Stop(f"--keep-days must be at least {MIN_KEEP_DAYS}: today's and yesterday's videos stay", EX_USAGE)
    if args.wait < 0 or args.max_mb_s < 0 or (args.limit is not None and args.limit < 0):
        raise Stop("--wait, --max-mb-s and --limit take numbers of 0 or more", EX_USAGE)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cameras, "video")):
        raise Stop(f"no camera videos in {cameras} (video/ is missing)", EX_USAGE)
    reachable(offsite)
    bad_before = run_.previous().get("bad_seen") or {}

    held = []
    try:
        if run_.dry_run:
            why = gate(heavy.now(), heavy.read_statuses(os.path.join(cameras, "status")))
            if why:
                run_.say(f"a real run would wait: {why}")
        else:
            fd = take_lock(os.path.join(cameras, LOCK))
            if fd is None:
                raise Stop("another cold-videos run is going", EX_LATER, record=False)
            held.append(fd)
            held.append(wait_to_start(cameras, args.wait, run_.say))
            run_.deadline = deadline_after(heavy.now())

        today = heavy.now().date()
        run_.cutoff = today - dt.timedelta(days=keep + 1)
        files, run_.kept = plan(cameras, run_.cutoff)
        if args.limit is not None:
            files = files[:args.limit]
        total = sum(size for _, size in files)
        run_.say(f"{len(files)} files ({gb(total):.2f} GB) of days up to {run_.cutoff.isoformat()} to send "
                 f"off-site (keeping {keep} finished days)")
        for why, n in sorted(run_.kept.items()):
            run_.say(f"staying: {n} files: {why}")
        if run_.dry_run:
            for rel, size in files:
                run_.say(f"would send {rel} ({size} bytes)")
            run_.left = len(files)
        else:
            send_new(files, cameras, offsite, Pace(args.max_mb_s), run_)

        try:
            stored = offsite.listing(within(run_.deadline, moving(0) * 10))
        except OffsiteError as err:
            reachable(offsite)
            raise Stop(f"the off-site storage's list failed ({err}), so nothing was checked against it", EX_FAILED)
        found = links(cameras)
        audit({rel: t for rel, t in found.items() if t.startswith(OFFSITE)}, stored, run_)
        olds = {rel: t for rel, t in found.items() if not t.startswith(OFFSITE)}
        if args.limit is not None:
            run_.old_left = len(olds)
            run_.say(f"old links: left alone (--limit); {len(olds)} still link to the cold drive")
        else:
            relink_old(olds, stored, offsite, run_, bad_before)
        return EX_FAILED if run_.failed or run_.offsite_missing else 0
    finally:
        for fd in reversed(held):
            os.close(fd)


def bring_back(rels, run_, max_mb_s):
    """Fetches off-site files back onto the VM's disk, with the other file of each camera-day, each
    checked against the bytes and sha256 in its link before it replaces the link. Returns the exit
    code."""
    cameras = run_.cameras
    offsite = offsite_settings()
    reachable(offsite)
    fd = take_lock(os.path.join(cameras, LOCK))
    if fd is None:
        raise Stop("a cold-videos run is going", EX_LATER)
    pace = Pace(max_mb_s)
    wanted = []
    for given in rels:
        rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.abspath(given), cameras) if os.path.isabs(given) else given
        for r in (rel, sibling(rel)):
            target = os.readlink(os.path.join(cameras, r)) if REL.fullmatch(r) and \
                os.path.islink(os.path.join(cameras, r)) else ""
            if r not in (w for w, _ in wanted) and (r == rel or OFFSITE_TARGET.fullmatch(target)):
                wanted.append((r, target))
    try:
        for rel, target in wanted:
            path = os.path.join(cameras, rel)
            m = OFFSITE_TARGET.fullmatch(target)
            if not m:
                run_.failed += 1
                run_.say(f"FAILED {rel}: not an off-site link in {cameras}" +
                         (" (a cold-drive link: it becomes an off-site link once its copy is proven)"
                          if target else ""))
                continue
            size, sha = int(m["bytes"]), m["sha"]
            free = heavy.free_gb(cameras)
            if free - gb(size) < heavy.FLOOR_GB + BACK_SPARE_GB:
                raise Stop(f"{free:.1f} GB free on the VM's disk: no room for {rel} above heavy's floor", EX_FAILED)
            tmp = hidden(path, BACK)
            try:
                with open(tmp, "wb") as f:
                    n, got = offsite.get(rel, f, pace, moving(size))
                    f.flush()
                    os.fsync(f.fileno())
                if (n, got) != (size, sha):
                    raise CheckFailed(f"what came back ({n} bytes, sha256 {got}) isn't what was sent")
                os.chmod(tmp, 0o644)
                os.replace(tmp, path)                    # one rename: the link or the file, never neither
            except (CheckFailed, OSError) as err:
                run_.failed += 1
                run_.say(f"FAILED {rel}: {err} (its link stays)")
                continue
            finally:
                if os.path.lexists(tmp):
                    os.remove(tmp)
            fsync_dir(os.path.dirname(path))
            run_.moved += 1
            run_.bytes += size
            run_.say(f"brought back {rel} ({size} bytes, sha256 {sha})")
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    return EX_FAILED if run_.failed else 0


def main(argv=None):
    try:
        args = parse(argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:])
    except SystemExit as err:
        return EX_USAGE if err.code else 0
    cameras = os.path.abspath(args.archive or os.path.dirname(heavy.STATUS_DIR))
    run_ = Run(cameras, args.dry_run)

    def terminated(_signum, _frame):
        raise Terminated()

    previous = signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, terminated)
    try:
        if args.bring_back:
            try:
                code = bring_back(args.bring_back, run_, args.max_mb_s)
            except Stop as stop:
                run_.say(f"bring-back stopped: {stop}")
                code = stop.code
            run_.say(f"brought back {run_.moved} files ({gb(run_.bytes):.2f} GB)"
                     + (f"; {run_.failed} failed" if run_.failed else ""))
            return code
        code = run(args, run_)
        return run_.finish(code)
    except Stop as stop:
        return run_.finish(stop.code, str(stop), stop.record)
    except (KeyboardInterrupt, Terminated):
        if args.bring_back:
            run_.say("bring-back interrupted; the file coming back stays off-site, behind its link")
            return EX_INT
        return run_.finish(EX_INT, "interrupted; the file being sent stays where it was")
    except Exception as err:                 # anything unforeseen still ends in the log and the state
        if args.bring_back:
            run_.say(f"bring-back stopped by an error: {err!r}")
            return EX_FAILED
        return run_.finish(EX_FAILED, f"stopped by an error: {err!r}")
    finally:
        signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, previous)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
